  ('lisp', 'cecear', 'A speech impediment characterized by the mispronunciation of sibilant consonants, such as ''s'' and ''z'', which are pronounced like ''th'' sounds.', 'He has a slight lisp that makes his ''s'' sound like ''th''.', 'B2', 'noun', 'general-vocabulary', 33355),
