  ('pulsar', 'pulsar', 'A highly magnetized, rotating neutron star that emits beams of electromagnetic radiation out of its magnetic poles, appearing as regular pulses when observed from Earth.', 'The pulsar rotates at an incredible speed of several hundred times per second.', 'C1', 'noun', 'science', 34824),
