  ('camphor', 'cânfora', 'A white, crystalline substance with a strong, characteristic odor, obtained from the wood of the camphor tree or synthesized. It is used in medicinal ointments, plastics, and as a moth repellent.', 'Camphor is often added to chest rubs to relieve congestion.', 'B2', 'noun', 'technical', 38466),
